.TH BASENAME 1.SH NAMEbasename, dirname \- the parts of a pathlist.SH SYNOPSIS\fBbasename\fRpath [suffix].br\fBdirname\fRpath.SH DESCRIPTION\fBbasename\fRprints\fIpath\fRwith everything up to the last slash removed, and\fIsuffix\fRtoo if the name ends with it:\fBbasename /dd/SRC/ls/ls.c .c\fRprints\fBls\fR.\fR.PP\fBdirname\fRprints the other half, everything before the last slash:\fBdirname /dd/SRC/ls/ls.c\fRprints\fB/dd/SRC/ls\fR.\fR.PPBoth are for shell scripts.  Martin Gregorie, 1994, from his sh75package..SH NOTESBoth need Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fR